# Next.js owns this file and rewrites it on every `next build` and `next dev`,
# reformatting the whole document its own way - short arrays expanded across
# lines where Prettier would collapse them, and the last line terminated CRLF on
# Windows. The two tools therefore disagree permanently, and the disagreement is
# invisible: `git status` reports the tree clean because Git normalises line
# endings away, so a build leaves a file that fails `format:check` and there is
# no diff to revert.
#
# Removing it from Prettier's remit is a boundary, not a suppression. Prettier
# never had a correctness opinion about this file - `tsc` does, and the gate
# runs `tsc` over it twice (tsconfig.json and tsconfig.tests.json). Letting a
# build tool own the formatting of its own config is the smaller evil than
# letting the gate fail on a file nobody edited.
#
# tsconfig.tests.json is deliberately NOT listed: no tool rewrites it, so it
# stays under Prettier like every other source file.
tsconfig.json